    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look for high-impact production today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (67.28) and **Sam Antonacci** (64.49). Despite a pending lineup, **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite start against Robbie Ray, as the park factors and favorable batting order outweigh the neutral platoon matchup. **Sam Antonacci** is our highest-projected value play today; facing Seth Lugo, his excellent .391 xwOBA and top-of-the-order usage drive a high-efficiency profile that makes him a priority start in our quest to bolster our stolen base totals. **Gunnar Henderson** (62.31) also projects well, benefitting significantly from wind blowing out at the park, which provides a meaningful boost to his power potential against Max Fried despite the difficult matchup.\n\nOur decision to bench **Brady House** (49.99) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73) highlights the razor-thin margins in our current rotation. **Brady House** fell just short of the cut because, while he offers solid park factors against Nick Lodolo, his projected efficiency was suppressed by a poor platoon split that the optimizer couldn't ignore. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is held back by the sheer difficulty of facing Griffin Jax, where his limited speed and tough matchup relegated him to the bench in favor of higher-floor plays like **Coby Mayo** (57.16), whose platoon advantage against the lefty Fried provides more utility for today\u2019s 5x5 needs.\n\nRisks remain, particularly concerning the elite arm of Shohei Ohtani, who threatens to cap the offensive ceiling for **Heliot Ramos** (41.12). **Heliot Ramos** is at the bottom of our starting threshold and is a high-risk candidate for an early hook if he fails to capitalize on his #5 spot. Furthermore, the reliance on assumed lineups for **Kyle Tucker**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Andy Pages** introduces volatility; if these players shift lower in their respective batting orders, their daily efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remaining on the IL, our roster depth is being tested, making it critical that **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** maximize their opportunities against their respective matchups to keep our team average competitive.",
